  ('5ec126d7-a260-5afe-8dad-d3df5b9f6638', '259b018a-f2e0-5558-b5a3-608da3d9ab21', 1, 'approved', 'The ruined stone city of Great Zimbabwe is in which present-day country?', 'Great Zimbabwe, built between the 11th and 15th centuries, lies near Masvingo in south-eastern Zimbabwe and gave the country its name.', 'history', array['ZW']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Great Zimbabwe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Zimbabwe"}]'::jsonb, 'aea8f663ea0d06a7186d7d63ebae3754b36448df18d0afe52ecd6f7e633f6309', now()),
  ('90b89dc4-c43d-511d-8d76-1b8405ac7015', '855694ad-1224-5b27-9fe8-8e0ed478cf67', 1, 'approved', 'Who was the first President of Kenya?', 'Jomo Kenyatta led Kenya to independence in 1963, first as Prime Minister and from 1964 as its first President.', 'history', array['KE']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Jomo Kenyatta","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jomo_Kenyatta"}]'::jsonb, 'b127354bb3baa9c213f49351c4d0eb7db6d1634a21beb4a2b24eca7010c28a81', now()),
  ('cf073b4d-5814-5e71-b082-1a47dd481639', 'e71185ba-c666-59ff-88b3-97310478d5a9', 1, 'approved', 'Which country defeated an Italian army at the Battle of Adwa in 1896?', 'Emperor Menelik II’s forces defeated Italy at Adwa in March 1896, securing Ethiopia’s independence.', 'history', array['ET']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Battle of Adwa","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Adwa"}]'::jsonb, '2a0878c96f9a7d00ca38625352541d228ebacf089762992916331c34f789881c', now()),
  ('bb7617f9-a56f-5c39-95fc-8b5e90b7924d', '15467b2a-e67c-5b2d-a3e4-f3baadabd3c5', 1, 'approved', 'Mansa Musa, famous for his wealth and his 1324 pilgrimage to Mecca, ruled which empire?', 'Mansa Musa ruled the Mali Empire in the early 14th century; his lavish pilgrimage made Mali famous across the Mediterranean world.', 'history', array['ML', 'WEST']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Mansa Musa","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mansa_Musa"}]'::jsonb, '325b275ab5ae6daacab9915451d3587412cb5c62eaaff19bccab316ca077e112', now()),
  ('2fb975c6-26b5-5070-b6d8-f990ae9dae21', 'e8652ded-e989-567e-b87b-133c4d4f7d8a', 1, 'approved', 'Who was the first Prime Minister of the independent Democratic Republic of the Congo in 1960?', 'Patrice Lumumba became Prime Minister at independence in June 1960; Joseph Kasa-Vubu was the first President.', 'history', array['CD']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Patrice Lumumba","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrice_Lumumba"}]'::jsonb, 'ae27e1b4b593f2fb8462898a750246c0880446696ec22c343371c94bf4e00708', now()),
  ('f0ff9d8a-a921-56ff-af61-899358d2ec0e', '90dd402f-c2cb-5caf-b0fd-218e04c9693e', 1, 'approved', 'In which year was the Organisation of African Unity (OAU) founded?', 'The OAU was founded in Addis Ababa on 25 May 1963. It was replaced by the African Union in 2002.', 'history', array['AFRICA']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Organisation of African Unity","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organisation_of_African_Unity"}]'::jsonb, 'da3808044b6f7b0efb7b87b2550ac270c0550014cf8e0e04de01f74ad7945284', now()),
  ('4b17c607-9b97-56c8-880d-d9a2002b170f', '95d3c82e-e68c-5db5-9206-379433d03aca', 1, 'approved', 'Which city was the capital of the Asante (Ashanti) Empire?', 'Kumasi, in present-day Ghana, was the capital of the Asante Empire and remains the seat of the Asantehene.', 'history', array['GH']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Ashanti Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashanti_Empire"}]'::jsonb, '717d3aea0681927287d106d1d60155c69308b391a98fa5736cf0fe6fc18c6fc1', now()),
  ('816a06ae-3f7d-561a-b2d2-57f2e6ef33b0', 'e89db7a3-46fb-5c01-846b-127c969ec807', 1, 'approved', 'The Zulu victory over British forces at Isandlwana in 1879 came during the reign of which king?', 'Cetshwayo kaMpande was king of the Zulu during the Anglo-Zulu War of 1879, which opened with the Zulu victory at Isandlwana.', 'history', array['ZA']::text[], 'hard', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Battle of Isandlwana","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Isandlwana"}]'::jsonb, 'e788d647d6232d75348b12ef7aaadefd4d328ac6a93db54aace38459a2a249e0', now()),
  ('702177ad-47a4-5516-b488-b39e63c6fcf6', '4e09a6c5-a634-5d07-9b50-285956e48bbe', 1, 'approved', 'The ancient Kingdom of Kush, whose kings ruled Egypt as its 25th Dynasty, was centred in which present-day country?', 'Kush was based along the Nile in present-day Sudan, with capitals at Kerma, Napata and Meroë.', 'history', array['SD']::text[], 'hard', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Kush","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kush"}]'::jsonb, 'a868f280b5714ecf479ebcacb0cfc6c4c39fb0c4c95fc02291a51b770442ae49', now()),
  ('c51d4ec1-f2c0-5a97-b906-2a2b7e10de0e', 'fde8ffd2-9538-5104-9696-7cc884b0f5b8', 1, 'approved', 'Which 17th-century queen of Ndongo and Matamba resisted Portuguese expansion in present-day Angola?', 'Nzinga Mbande ruled Ndongo and Matamba and fought Portuguese colonial expansion for decades.', 'history', array['AO']::text[], 'hard', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Nzinga of Ndongo and Matamba","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nzinga_of_Ndongo_and_Matamba"}]'::jsonb, 'cbfee64494c8847102d4b7112db67f2755da8f3bce6b4e6c5f87c83f4dbba4c6', now()),
  ('77b9b87c-2fd9-5b89-9b9a-c0ff72834b59', 'a61d8d84-108b-512a-8135-51d246821e1b', 1, 'approved', 'The ancient Kingdom of Aksum, which minted its own coins, was in present-day Ethiopia and which other country?', 'Aksum, a major trading power from around the 1st century AD, covered what is now Eritrea and northern Ethiopia.', 'history', array['ET', 'ER']::text[], 'hard', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Aksum","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Aksum"}]'::jsonb, 'dbb5276955756fac0bfb62dddb61976691107a106b125bcba92c710f29162e3e', now()),
  ('ae6988e7-3cef-5afb-bc70-b877b16263f9', '6a8d6423-e104-5ad8-8dc4-81c2aecd5984', 1, 'approved', 'What is the capital city of Nigeria?', 'Abuja replaced Lagos as Nigeria’s capital in 1991. Lagos remains the largest city.', 'geography', array['NG']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Abuja","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abuja"}]'::jsonb, '374dd8cc0b5c19a9a3de53950b34fde72a6e3a1b511e22e4de04e9c2db4d662a', now()),
  ('2340d80e-04a8-5872-9bb1-ede657cfa850', 'a6d88c28-ebc0-5a33-8df4-6d1171f4849e', 1, 'approved', 'What is the capital city of Egypt?', 'Cairo, on the Nile, is Egypt’s capital and one of the largest cities in Africa.', 'geography', array['EG']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Cairo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cairo"}]'::jsonb, '4e32cddb6307a18f8e87a9637aa671a815b8191c2d5c23193fd6707101d4335f', now()),
  ('7fdaa073-80d8-539f-87bc-389fa933bfa8', 'af3343db-575c-5ba3-bc90-a8c1ab1b8ad9', 1, 'approved', 'Which is the largest country in Africa by area?', 'Algeria, at about 2.38 million km², has been Africa’s largest country since South Sudan separated from Sudan in 2011.', 'geography', array['DZ']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Algeria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algeria"}]'::jsonb, 'f4448f4d783efa4959bd9736f305e1d47cfbc4c298617b9989987096d6129154', now()),
  ('aaf11a9d-2fa4-509e-bbb9-57d8e634f6b2', 'd304c3aa-bd94-58f3-a7aa-61a177747482', 1, 'approved', 'Victoria Falls lies on the border between Zambia and which country?', 'Victoria Falls, on the Zambezi River, sits on the border of Zambia and Zimbabwe. Its local name is Mosi-oa-Tunya.', 'geography', array['ZM', 'ZW']::text[], 'easy', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Victoria Falls","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_Falls"}]'::jsonb, 'bed46ae70fe4d2fc2ccd97855cdd3fa1833e2b827f53c1f1d068a3d669c0995e', now()),
  ('6bf6896b-d0d9-57d2-bf3a-aa30b5c29de2', '6a27341c-5e84-5ba8-8e5c-734af2eaa601', 1, 'approved', 'Lake Victoria is shared by Uganda, Kenya and which other country?', 'Lake Victoria, Africa’s largest lake by area, is divided between Tanzania, Uganda and Kenya.', 'geography', array['TZ', 'UG', 'KE']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Lake Victoria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Victoria"}]'::jsonb, 'c10fa50b37d4ee3eef81c34b66a1baff48f6565ff56c76498f442a2d3da7aecd', now()),
  ('eb366abf-ac10-5c76-a535-1732f2ea7b27', 'd83175fe-7576-5d5c-b6ee-0a42d0b4c1ef', 1, 'approved', 'What is the capital city of Senegal?', 'Dakar, on the Cap-Vert peninsula, is Senegal’s capital. Bamako is the capital of Mali.', 'geography', array['SN']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Dakar","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakar"}]'::jsonb, 'e9ce6dd20d2503f89f2b17e1ff7671408902e40d3d05be059dc6a878575a13e9', now()),
  ('af6dda68-60bf-5fe5-844f-543147797589', 'e6c199d0-ddaf-5cfb-936c-b58ac0c7e996', 1, 'approved', 'Which island country in the Indian Ocean has Victoria as its capital?', 'Seychelles is made up of 115 islands; its capital, Victoria, is on the island of Mahé.', 'geography', array['SC']::text[], 'medium', 'all', array['starter-set', 'needs-review']::text[], 'en', '[{"title":"Wikipedia: Seychelles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seychelles"}]'::jsonb, 'fe1e31e90c362a9ee9257c9cb09981e0cdedb350a772831a82ab6906cd366c8f', now()),
